{"t": 1794105438.6873631, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*Incident update \u2014 checkout / payment gateway (alert AG-7731)*\n\n*Symptom:* Gateway 4xx rate 38% for service=checkout since 07:41 UTC; charges rejected with 400.\n\n*Root cause:* Gateway API switched to 2026-11 (strict amounts) at 07:41:05 UTC. It now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents), but checkout was sending a decimal EUR amount. Error body: `invalid_amount: amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34`.\n\n*Fix:* `checkout/gateway.py` \u2014 `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents (Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP), e.g. 12.34 EUR -> `{\"amount\": 1234, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}`.\n\n*Next:* Deploy checkout and watch the gateway 4xx rate. Code fix is in place locally; production is not yet updated."}, "ok": true}
